    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on May 21st hinges on two high-ceiling matchups against Agnos. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear headliner today with a massive 87.14 efficiency score; batting second against a pitcher with a 5.15 xERA, his ability to leverage sprint speed for extra bases\u2014coupled with an elite 0.376 xwOBA\u2014makes him an auto-start. **Gabriel Moreno** also benefits from the soft Agnos matchup, earning a 65.19 score as he occupies the back half of the order. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains a priority start at 64.53, as his leadoff spot in the order provides a 10% boost that outweighs the marginal risk presented by a lefty-lefty matchup against Peterson.\n\nWe have strategically deployed **Kyle Karros** in the UTIL spot, as his 60.61 score reflects a favorable 4.55 xERA opponent in Rodriguez and a beneficial platoon split that keeps him ahead of our bench options. **Tyler Soderstrom** (59.99) and **Austin Riley** (56.25) round out the core, with **Austin Riley** specifically fighting through a poor BvP history and a slower delivery profile from Alcantara, though his upside remains higher than the remaining depth on our bench. **Travis Bazzana** (46.61) represents our most marginal start; while his platoon edge against Mize provides a baseline, his proximity to the 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold bears watching. \n\nRegarding roster management, the decision to bench **Mickey Moniak** was straightforward as he is out of the starting lineup, but we continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains sidelined on the IL. With **Josh Naylor** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** off-day participants, our bench depth is intentionally thin to maximize game caps for those active. We are keeping a close eye on **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Carson Williams** for potential late-week pivots should any of today's starters see their status shift due to weather or late-scratch announcements.",
